    description: "FILED BY ADR-0049 §\"Open work\" step 1. BLOCKS every row move in this family.\n\nTHE PROBLEM IS THAT NOBODY CAN COUNT THIS FAMILY. Four independent counts, four\nanswers, all produced by people trying:\n\n  37 rows / 9 languages   WI-johuk's headline claim\n  52 rows                 WI-johuk's OWN enumeration, summed\n  63 rows                 48 launch+route-DSL, plus a 15-row `accept` family\n  75 rows / 13 languages  a consistent membership rule via the production loader\n\nThey disagree because until ADR-0049 there was no written membership rule to\ncount against, so each sweep invented one. ADR-0049 ruling 1 supplies it:\n\n  Does this call return -- or write into a caller-visible location -- a value\n  whose content is chosen by the party on the far side of the boundary?\n\nWHAT TO DO. Re-run the census against that test, with the PRODUCTION loader\n(`_rows`-style merged view: all catalogues, `_CATALOG_PARENTS` inheritance,\nshipped default overlays), case-insensitively, over EVERY boundary that\nauto-derives a source -- net_recv, ipc_recv, db_read -- not just net_recv.\nClassify each hit into ADR-0049 ruling 4's four shapes. Emit a table: row,\nlanguage, catalogue file, shape, verdict.\n\nINSTRUMENT DISCIPLINE (this family has burned three sweeps already). A\nname-based sweep with an incomplete vocabulary does not fail, it reports clean:\nINV-nular's direction sweep carried the verb `respond` and missed the noun\n`responseLBS` across fifteen catalogues; the F2 socket gate is blind to Go twice\nover (hardcoded 9-language scope AND a case-sensitive predicate against a\nlanguage that capitalises exports); and WI-johuk itself omits erlang, rust and\nc/cpp -- the same hardcoded-9 defect it cites INV-kanuk for. Parametrise over\nthe tree's own language list, do not hardcode one. Report the denominator.\n\nKNOWN OMISSIONS from WI-johuk's list, already confirmed present:\n  erlang   gen_tcp.accept, ssl.transport_accept, httpd.start/start_service\n  rust     std::net::TcpListener.accept\n  c/cpp    sys/socket.accept\n  go       echo/v4.Echo.Start/StartTLS\n`accept` is 11 languages and is NOT family (ADR-0049 ruling 4) -- count it\nseparately so a family-wide retag cannot take it along."  # d8fe
    fields: {}  # d8fe
