- op: discuss  # d6bd
  at: '2026-08-29T23:36:55Z'  # d6bd
  by: agent  # d6bd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d6bd
  clock: 4  # d6bd
  nonce: d6bd  # d6bd
  message: "CENSUS COMPLETE for the three boundaries that carry the family. Full artifact: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/hazop_census_08292026/RESULT.md\n\nDENOMINATOR: 804 language-facing / 608 own rows across the five boundaries that auto-derive a taint source (net_recv, db_read, ipc_recv, env_read, host_info_read). Production loader, all 15 catalogues, parents and shipped overlays, case-folded.\n\nRESULT — 131 DEFERRED CROSSINGS, against the 37 this item was filed to re-count.\n  net_recv        138 own   100% adjudicated    80 deferred\n  db_read         130 own   100% adjudicated    38 deferred\n  ipc_recv         64 own   100% adjudicated    13 deferred\n  env_read         60 own   NOT adjudicated\n  host_info_read  216 own   NOT adjudicated\n  total           608       332 (55%)          131\n\nenv_read and host_info_read are NOT done and this says so rather than implying coverage. They are lowest-risk by inspection (platform.system, os.release) and inspection is precisely what the critic below refuted.\n\nTHE INSTRUMENT HAD TO BE ABANDONED MID-CENSUS, WHICH IS THE METHODOLOGICAL RESULT. A wide case-folded vocabulary flagged 129 of 608. A completeness critic — 40 random NON-candidates — found 4 misses: WebSocket.onClose, dets.traverse, django.db.models.exclude and values_list. A ~10% miss rate extrapolating to ~48 missed rows. So the three boundaries that matter were ENUMERATED 100% rather than sampled. Third measured demonstration that names cannot scope this family: the direction sweep carried the verb 'respond' but not the noun 'response'; the F2 gate missed go by case AND scope; the candidate vocabulary missed lazy combinators and callback-delivered reads. The common cause is not bad vocabularies — 'does this call hand you the data' is not a property of the name.\n\nSIX SHAPES, NOT FOUR. ADR-0049 ruling 4 names SETUP / LAUNCH / ACCEPT / REGISTER. The census found two more that fail ruling 1 identically, so the RULING covers them and only its table is short:\n  HANDLE   returns a handle, not data — sqlite3.connect, Connection.prepareStatement, bufio.NewReader, sys.stdin, System.in, std.cin, dets.open_file, Socket.getInputStream. The largest unnamed shape, and why db_read/ipc_recv looked transfer-heavy.\n  LAZY     returns an unexecuted query or iterator — django.db.models.{filter,exclude,annotate,values_list,select_related,prefetch_related,iterator,...} x12, Ecto.Repo.stream, TypedQuery.getResultStream, EntityManager.getReference, TcpListener.incoming, iterdump.\n\nFINDINGS NO PRIOR COUNT HAD.\n1. Django's lazy QuerySet combinators are TWELVE rows of db_read. INV-nular F3 RULED this exact shape for Django and the rows were never swept against the ruling.\n2. ftplib.FTP.retrbinary / retrlines hand the data to a CALLBACK; the caller receives nothing. The name says 'retr', which is why a direction sweep keeps them and a reader agrees with the sweep.\n3. Channel.channelRead (swift) is the ONE arrival-scope row in the entire tree — the handler method where bytes land, the shape WI-ritog's Tier 2 needs, existing exactly once across fifteen catalogues.\n\nMISDECLARATIONS OF OTHER KINDS, found in passing and filed separately — not deferred crossings: inet.gethostname is net_recv and reads the LOCAL hostname; NSNotificationCenter.removeObserver: x2 under ipc_recv un-register and receive nothing; os.wait/wait3/wait4/waitid/waitpid under ipc_recv return a process exit status, not IPC payload; sqlite3.Connection.backup under db_read WRITES; ets.info and mnesia.table_info return table metadata, not stored rows.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR SEQUENCING. 131 rows across three boundaries is materially bigger than the 'all 37 move together' ADR-0049 anticipated, and it now touches the verdict path in db_read and ipc_recv as well as net_recv. Retagging all 131 in one diff would be high-risk. Recommended: tranches BY SHAPE — SETUP and LAUNCH first (clearest, and what INV-kanuk needs), then HANDLE and LAZY. That is sequencing the mechanical application of a made ruling against a complete census, not re-adjudicating it. Owner call pending."  # d6bd
